Neverlur
========

Neverlur is a post-quantum fork of the Alpenhorn friend-discovery service
for metadata-private messaging.

Upstream project
----------------

This codebase derives from:

  Alpenhorn
  https://github.com/vuvuzela/alpenhorn

Original authors:

  Copyright (c) 2015-2019 David Lazar
  with contributions from collaborators at MIT CSAIL.

Upstream paper: David Lazar and Nickolai Zeldovich, "Alpenhorn: Bootstrapping
Secure Communication without Leaking Metadata", OSDI 2016.
https://davidlazar.org/papers/alpenhorn.pdf

Fork
----

Neverlur is maintained at https://github.com/oluies/neverlur.
The fork was created to migrate the friend-discovery layer to post-quantum
cryptographic primitives (hybrid X25519+ML-KEM-768 key agreement, hybrid
Ed25519+ML-DSA-65 signatures) while preserving the original protocol design,
threat model, and license.

All files retained from the upstream project keep their original copyright
notices ("Copyright 2015 David Lazar. All rights reserved." and similar) and
license headers. Modifications and new files carry their own copyright
notices alongside the upstream notice where appropriate.

